 SE: The 'image' parameter from user input in $_GET array is directly used to construct the file path for reading image file.
BL: $imageName = $_GET['image'];
serveImage($imageName);
BUG FOUND: YES

Explanation:
This code is vulnerable to Path Traversal attack (CWE-22) as it uses user-supplied input ($_GET['image']) to construct the file path ($imageName) without proper validation or sanitization. An attacker can manipulate the input to access files outside of the intended directory ("/var/www/html/images/") by using "../" in the input. This can lead to unauthorized file access or reading sensitive information.

