Explanation:
This code is vulnerable to a path traversal attack (CWE-22) because it uses user input ($_GET['image']) to construct a file path ($fullPath) without proper validation or sanitization. An attacker could potentially manipulate the 'image' parameter to access files outside of the intended directory ('/var/www/html/images/'), including sensitive files in other parts of the system. To mitigate this risk, you should validate and sanitize the user input to ensure it only contains allowed characters and does not attempt to traverse the file system.

